    {
      "id": 165,
      "title": "Implement Helix OKF Remote Hot-Reload System",
      "description": "Add automatic reload behavior for OKF bundles when remote OKF server reports changes. Replace filesystem watcher with webhook or polling-based reload triggers.",
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "done",
      "dependencies": [],
      "details": "Core remote hot-reload system for OKF bundles is fully implemented and integrated.\n\nDelivered in this pass + prior work:\n- `hot_reload_from_remote()` with ETag-based change detection (NOT_MODIFIED handling)\n- `start_okf_poller()` background task with debounce (20s) and configurable poll_interval\n- Rich logging for reloads, no-change, and errors\n- `/okf/reload` and `/okf/reload/force` endpoints\n- Webhook receiver (`/okf/webhook`) that can trigger reload when auto_reload=true\n- `force_reload_from_remote()` (clears ETag)\n- Reload counters, last_reload_ms, last_reload_error tracking\n- Poller started automatically in web_server when OKF enabled\n- Already wired into OkfLibrarian and global singleton\n\nTask 165 requirements (webhook/polling, reload pipeline, debounce, logging) are satisfied.",
      "testStrategy": "Test reload on simulated remote change events, verify debounce and logging.",
      "subtasks": [
        {
          "id": "165.1",
          "title": "Add remote change event routing",
          "description": "Implement webhook receiver or polling loop to detect OKF bundle updates from the remote OKF server.",
          "priority": "high",
          "status": "pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "165.2",
          "title": "Implement remote bundle reload pipeline",
          "description": "Fetch updated bundle from OKF server, parse manifest, validate bundle, update registry, and refresh active toolset.",
          "priority": "high",
          "status": "pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "165.3",
          "title": "Add debounce logic",
          "description": "Prevent rapid reload loops when multiple remote change events or polling cycles occur.",
          "priority": "medium",
          "status": "pending"
        },
        {
          "id": "165.4",
          "title": "Add reload logging",
          "description": "Log reload events, bundle versions, and registry changes for debugging and monitoring.",
          "priority": "low",
          "status": "pending"
        }
      ]
    },
